                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0565b917-0f68-3ead-8acc-74aaab075943",
                        "entry_id": "c8fb6b70-17fa-3c9e-9989-982d20f89a27",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any speech disorder."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "83e083fd-7b7d-4a5a-9ff1-35baa1ccdf96",
                                "sense_id": "0565b917-0f68-3ead-8acc-74aaab075943",
                                "text": "Conversely a correct thought may be defectively expressed, but as soon as the formation of thoughts is disturbed it becomes a question of dyslogia and logopathy, or, as some would say, of logoneurosis, since every movement of thought takes place through the nerve-substance. The two ideas of logoneurosis and lalopathy consequently do not cover each other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a80faec-24c0-49fa-a1de-9876eb50771c",
                                "sense_id": "0565b917-0f68-3ead-8acc-74aaab075943",
                                "text": "Stammering. stuttering, apthongia, spasmodic hesitation. and “nervous speech” belong to the domain of lalopathy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "254226e2-d8ce-4388-8428-977af5fc7d9b",
                                "sense_id": "0565b917-0f68-3ead-8acc-74aaab075943",
                                "text": "As for the symptom of brain metastasis, dyskinesia showed the highest incidence, being seen in 5 cases (56%), followed by headache, nausea, lalopathy, dysopia and aystaria."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12889569-b646-4532-9449-394714749aa9",
                                "sense_id": "0565b917-0f68-3ead-8acc-74aaab075943",
                                "text": "Myasthenoid syndrome (somnolence, hypotonia, ataxy, lalopathy) due to acute intentional poisoning with 0.250g of Diazepan was observed in a child."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
